    "overview": "replayd is a compact, calm workbench for following recorded evidence. Cool neutral surfaces, clear blue actions and restrained severity colors keep dense debugging information readable. Familiar sidebar navigation, project cards and tables support the owner's chosen product language.\n\nThe interface carries a developer from project to issue, event, replay and resolution. A persistent workspace frame establishes location while the main area focuses on the current task. Settings and account screens share the same controls, spacing and material character. The visual authority is the built dashboard, especially `dashboard/app/assets/css/main.css`, its shared UI components and layout; product purpose is recorded in `PRODUCT.md`.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Compact, readable information density.",
      "Cool surfaces with subtle borders.",
      "Blue actions and explicit semantic severity.",
      "System typography and conventional controls.",
      "Equivalent light and dark themes."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Paired Theme Rule",
        "body": "Change text, backgrounds and borders together through semantic tokens. Primary actions use white text in light mode and dark canvas text in dark mode; inspect both states rather than assuming a text utility remains readable.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Overlay Depth Rule",
        "body": "Use a shadow to identify a surface above the current task, not to decorate each content card.",
        "section": "elevation"
